 ["PR 101 through commit c22c2deaca6f1806bd2b378a097bc6498fb3581d"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datahike :datascript]
 :root-cause
 "Dafny's abstract set insertion counter was incorrectly treated as a target-runtime cost model. Dafny 4.11 Java copied HashSet values on immutable union, JavaScript used array sets/maps, JavaScript eager sequence suffixes copied represented values, and executable scan validation evaluated a pairwise quantified strict-order predicate as a quadratic nested loop. Functional semantics remained correct while generated target work and allocation became quadratic."
 :fix
 "Keep pairwise strict ordering as the Dafny specification, prove it equivalent to an adjacent-pair predicate, and use only the linear predicate in executable validation. Deterministically patch generated Java sets/maps to Clojure persistent collections and generated JavaScript sets/maps/sequences to Immutable HAMTs plus persistent virtual-length sequence views. Hash the patch boundary into the manifest and gate persistence, structural equality, collisions, fixed-heap completion, and target scaling."
